;; Physics and literature priors on recipe coefficients (docs/ESSENTIALS.md
;; section 4, step 5 of section 8; bead bnm-1pq.6), read by bnm.recipes.
;;
;; Each recipe is one coefficient: input per unit of output, in :unit. Its
;; prior is a central value :mean and a 90% range [:lo :hi]; on :scale :log
;; (the default) the mean is the median and the range sets the log sd,
;; (ln hi - ln lo) / 3.29; on :scale :logit (shares) the same on the log
;; odds. :floor is the thermodynamic or stoichiometric minimum, with
;; :floor-basis saying why; 0 where physics sets none (the posterior is
;; then only kept positive). The prior holds at :ref-year; :drift is a
;; yearly change of the log (a learning or chemistry trend) applied from
;; :drift-from on (flat before it), :step the log sd of the coefficient's
;; random walk per year. :sources say which observations update it
;; (bnm.recipes/observations); a recipe with none keeps its prior (and
;; drift). :regions lists where it is filtered: EXIOBASE region codes (ISO
;; alpha-2 for countries, WA WE WF WL WM for the rest of the world) and
;; WLD; :exio-all means every EXIOBASE region with data.
;;
;; Unit conventions (marked per recipe):
;;   t     metric tonne; kt = 1e3 t; Mt = 1e6 t.
;;   GJ    net (lower) calorific value unless marked gross. Fuels in
;;         tonnes convert at the IPCC 2006 defaults in bnm.supply/ncv
;;         (natural gas 48.0 GJ/t, other bituminous coal 25.8, coking coal
;;         28.2, lignite 11.9). UNSD reports natural gas in TJ gross: x 0.9
;;         to net.
;;   MWh   electricity, 3.6 GJ; 1 TJ = 277.8 MWh.
;;   per GW   per GW of installed (nameplate) capacity, DC for PV.
;;   per kWh  per kWh of Li-ion cell capacity.
;;   NH3   per t of ammonia; EXIOBASE's N-fertiliser tonnage is read as t
;;         of NH3 equivalent (docs/ESSENTIALS.md 4 does the same: 0.64 t
;;         of gas per t in Germany); this unit assumption is part of the
;;         source's error.
;;
;; Sources (implemented in bnm.recipes; :sd0 is the observation's log sd
;; before the data teach it):
;;   :exio      EXIOBASE hybrid 2011 physical coefficient of :output from
;;              :inputs ({code factor}; :conv :ncv turns tonnes of fuel to
;;              TJ first), times :factor; known 2014. With :price, also
;;              each other pxp year's value-share-implied coefficient:
;;              a(2011) x s(y)/s(2011) x [P_out(y)/P_out(2011)] /
;;              [P_in(y)/P_in(2011)], s the summed value share of
;;              :share-inputs, P the BACI HS92 world unit values of the
;;              listed HS6 codes; known y + 3.
;;   :exio-ammonia  the same for ammonia, split by route (gas reforming,
;;              coal gasification) with the prior route intensities.
;;   :exio-power-share  fossil share of electricity output, EXIOBASE 2011.
;;   :stage     ratio of world stage outputs, data/derived/supply/
;;              stages.csv (:num stage over :den stage), :adjust scaling
;;              a country's :num quantity, times :factor.
;;   :bf-coal   UNSD coking coal into coke ovens, attributed to blast
;;              furnaces by coke into them over coke made, plus coal
;;              injected, over pig iron (stages.csv), per country.
;;   :unsd-heat-rate  UNSD fuel into electricity and CHP plants, less the
;;              fuel of their heat (heat out / 0.9), over electricity from
;;              that fuel, x 3.6; known year + 2.
;;   :unsd-ratio  ratio of two UNSD series (:num / :den).
;;   :fao-nutrient  FAOSTAT agricultural use of a nutrient x :factor (the
;;              share of wheat, maize and rice, and the element's mass
;;              fraction) over their production (FAOSTAT food balances,
;;              rice milled); known + 2.
;;   :screen    an observation more than :screen-sds predictive sds (the
;;              prior's and the source's :sd0 together, on the filter's
;;              scale) from the prior is a flag (a unit or routing error,
;;              PRINCIPLES 10), counted and not used.

{:start 1995
 :end 2025
 ;; the filter runs from :from, so the 1990s data known by 1995 inform it
 :from 1990
 :screen-sds 4.0
 :literature
 {:iea-minerals "IEA (2021). The Role of Critical Minerals in Clean Energy Transitions. Paris. https://www.iea.org/reports/the-role-of-critical-minerals-in-clean-energy-transitions"
  :iea-ammonia "IEA (2021). Ammonia Technology Roadmap. Paris. https://www.iea.org/reports/ammonia-technology-roadmap"
  :iea-cement "IEA & WBCSD-CSI (2018). Technology Roadmap: Low-Carbon Transition in the Cement Industry. https://www.iea.org/reports/technology-roadmap-low-carbon-transition-in-the-cement-industry"
  :worldbank "Hund, K., La Porta, D., Fabregas, T.P., Laing, T. & Drexhage, J. (2020). Minerals for Climate Action: The Mineral Intensity of the Clean Energy Transition. World Bank."
  :watari "Watari, T., McLellan, B.C., Giurco, D., Dominish, E., Yamasue, E. & Nansai, K. (2019). Total material requirement for the global energy transition to 2050. Resources, Conservation and Recycling 148:91-103. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resconrec.2019.05.015"
  :worrell "Worrell, E., Price, L., Neelis, M., Galitsky, C. & Zhou, N. (2008). World Best Practice Energy Intensity Values for Selected Industrial Sectors. LBNL-62806. https://doi.org/10.2172/927032"
  :fruehan "Fruehan, R.J., Fortini, O., Paxton, H.W. & Brindle, R. (2000). Theoretical Minimum Energies to Produce Steel for Selected Conditions. US DOE / Energetics. https://doi.org/10.2172/769470"
